DESCRIPTION:Step inside the House of Happy Walls Museum for a fascinating
  exploration of Jack London’s personal medicine case and the remarkable 
 story it reveals about his life\, health\, and writing. Dating from 1909
 –1910\, the black leather Squibb medicine case on display in the museum 
 contains 22 glass vials with metal screw caps and drugs mostly in tablet f
 orm. The drugs in the case include various opioid and non-opioid analgesic
 s\, antipyretics (fever reducers)\, anti-inflammatories\, drugs for respir
 atory d
